  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contract obligations in Massachusetts for FY2027 to date total $141M. Obligations fell 99.3% year over year. Federal award activity shows 4,166 awards with an average award size of $33.8K. Historical annual obligations illustrate a sharp contrast: FY22 was $17.9B, FY23 was $18.3B, FY24 was $17.8B, FY25 was $19.3B, and FY26 was $19.9B, compared with $141M in FY27 to date. The top buying agencies in FY2027 to date are the Department of Veterans Affairs with $89M, the Department of the Treasury with $20.4M, and the Department of Transportation with $20.2M. The top vendors in FY2027 to date include CRANE & CO., INC. with $20.4M, RAYTHEON COMPANY with $11.9M, and FEDEX SUPPLY CHAIN DISTRIBUTION SYSTEM, INC. with $10.8M. Leading industries by obligation in FY2027 to date are Paper Mills with $19.2M and Engineering Services with $18.1M. All figures are contract obligations and current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date).",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How did federal obligations in Massachusetts change year over year?",
        "body": "FY2027 to date obligations in Massachusetts are $141M. Obligations fell 99.3% year over year. Annual obligations before FY27 were $17.9B in FY22, $18.3B in FY23, $17.8B in FY24, $19.3B in FY25, and $19.9B in FY26. The FY27 to date figure is a partial fiscal year total."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and industries account for most FY2027 to date spending in Massachusetts?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $89M in FY2027 to date. The Department of the Treasury obligated $20.4M and the Department of Transportation obligated $20.2M. Paper Mills is the largest industry by obligations with $19.2M, followed by Engineering Services with $18.1M."
      }
